        "signature": "",
        "thinking": "I'm weighing the moral dilemma and deciding on an answer, since it's a personal-choice question where I can give my honest view. Stealing is wrong even when it's invisible, though the harm to the owner is modest, so I'm leaning toward choice A and will keep the explanation brief.\n\n",
        "type": "thinking"
      },
      {
        "citations": null,
        "text": "**A) Leave the money.**\n\nBeing unseen doesn't change whether taking it is wrong. The money belongs to someone else, and taking it without consent treats them as a means to my own relief. The owner's loss would be real, even if they could absorb it. And the fact that I'd never be caught only means I'd escape consequences, not that the act would be right.",
